# Wiki schema for ${vault_id}

Auto-generated by `wiki-init`. Edit as needed; `vault_id` is REQUIRED
(ADR-002 §D1.1) and MUST match the SQLite vault row in the index DB.

**Optional `index_db:` (TASK 022)** — by default every vault shares ONE global DB
(partitioned by `vault_id`). To make this vault **self-contained** (DB travels with it,
gitignored, rebuildable), add e.g. `index_db: .wiki/index.db` to the frontmatter above (or run
`wiki-init … --local`). Resolution precedence: `--db-path` flag > `index_db` > global. The path
is vault-root-**relative** (portable, and contained — a symlink/`..` escape is refused). Use an
ABSOLUTE path only when the vault is cloud-synced (iCloud/Dropbox) since SQLite must NOT live inside
a byte-syncing folder (WAL/shm corruption — the iCloud guard rejects it); an absolute `index_db`
requires the explicit env opt-in **`WIKI_ALLOW_ABSOLUTE_INDEX_DB=1`** (because this file travels with
the vault, an absolute path from a cloned/synced vault could otherwise redirect writes). A local-DB
vault is an **island**: `--vault all` spans only its own DB; a nested sub-vault with its own
`index_db` routes to a different DB (nearest WIKI_SCHEMA.md wins).

## Optional per-vault config (override the built-in `${layout}` layout)

Two optional files under `<vault>/.wiki/` let a real mixed vault tune behaviour
without code changes:

- **`.wiki/layout.yaml`** — override the layout grammar (e.g. extend `ignore`
  to keep `_inbox/`, `_daily/`, attachment dirs, or private subtrees OUT of the
  search index). `ignore` is **additive** — just list your own globs; the built-in
  layout's `ignore` (`.obsidian/**`, `.trash/**`, `_templates/**`, `**/*.base`) is
  kept automatically (union). (`paths`/`ref_extraction`, by contrast, REPLACE.)
- **`.wiki/sync.yaml`** — configure `wiki-sync` (the format-aware, tag-routed
  ingest dispatcher): `zones`, `exclude`, `tag_namespace` (default `wiki`),
  `extensions`. Drop transcripts / office docs / scanned PDFs into a zone and
  `wiki-sync` auto-routes each file (convert+OCR / ingest / upsert / skip).

Per-note routing tags (namespace `wiki`, precedence **skip > raw > keep >
default**): `#wiki/raw` (full ingest → distil), `#wiki/skip` (never touch),
`#wiki/keep` (rescue a `.md` from an excluded zone). See the obsidian-llm-wiki
manual → *Working with documents* for the full recipe.
